From: MarkJiang-maji <chiang142536@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:57:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] Deploy the v71 billing monitor from the repo so .4 can
 run it

The admin Home and User billing pages only worked on clusters where v71
had been installed by hand. On .4 the rate API returned 404, Prometheus
was unreachable on 32049, and the billing metrics did not exist.

cgu/monitor/v71 holds the exporter, rules and both rate ConfigMaps, and
cgu/monitor/kustomization.yaml now includes it, so apply.sh installs it.
prom_v2.py is the only copy of the program; kustomize generates its
ConfigMap, replacing prom_v2_script.yaml.

The rate ConfigMaps are CREATE_ONLY in preserve_live_state.py, so a
redeploy keeps rates edited on the web page.

apply-prometheus-settings.sh sets NodePort 32049 and 360 days of
retention by patching, as helm values on .6 are empty. .6 stays on 180
days. Changing retention without a PVC deletes stored data, so the script
stops unless CONFIRM_DATA_LOSS=yes is set.

kubectl diff against live: .6 differs only in the two fallback rate
defaults in prom_v2.py, with no Deployment change; .4 adds 10 new objects
and changes nothing existing. The v53 prom.yaml has no diff on either.
